cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use a result, please cite the paper it comes from (listed under references); to cite the code and measurement artifacts themselves, cite this record."
type: software
title: "deterministic-int8-llm-inference: measurement programme and reproducibility companion for two papers on cross-kernel INT8 inference numerics"
abstract: >-
  The pre-registration, measurement harness, analysis code and measurement
  artifacts for two papers. The Integer Alibi (arXiv:2608.13756) localizes
  cross-kernel divergence in INT8-quantized LLM inference to the epilogue, using
  the exactness of INT32 accumulation under a verified bound. Deterministic LLM
  Inference Across GPU Kernels (arXiv:2609.00363) measures what a tolerance-based
  conformance suite detects under injected faults, and the cost of serving with
  power-of-two weight scales. Re-analysis runs on a CPU.
